2026-10-15T16:06:50.1876225Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1949558Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1956702Z [0m
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1957050Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1959015Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1959353Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1959522Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1960510Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1960759Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1960902Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1961192Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1961333Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1961703Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1962092Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1962409Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1962686Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1962835Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1962971Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963160Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963300Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963578Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963683Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963759Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1963885Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1964101Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1964487Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1964729Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1964839Z I will:
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1965211Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1965567Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1965988Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1966416Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1966703Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1966925Z  - install Nix in to /nix
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1967134Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1967442Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-15T16:06:50.1967718Z    /root
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2397863Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2398491Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2405787Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2406589Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2406903Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2407328Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2407754Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2421632Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2422627Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2429341Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2430088Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2430409Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2430556Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2430703Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2430959Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2431178Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2431691Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2431865Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2431944Z If you would like to
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2432246Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2432434Z 
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2432621Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2433008Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-15T16:06:50.2433150Z 
